{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"p adic valuation p adic valuation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md","fileName":"p-Adic Valuation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"p-Adic Valuation","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-15 10:15\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Ultrametric Hierarchy and Information]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ultrametric Hierarchy and Information","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"p adic valuation p adic valuation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md","fileName":"p-Adic Valuation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"p-Adic Valuation","heading":"p-Adic Valuation","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"For a chosen prime p, the p-adic valuation of a nonzero integer is the exponent of the highest power of p dividing it. For a rational numerator divided by denominator, the valuation is the numerator's exponent minus the denominator's. The associated p-adic norm is p raised to the negative valuation.\n\nThis reverses ordinary magnitude intuitions: a number divisible by a very high power of p is small in the p-adic norm. The resulting non-Archimedean distance expresses closeness through shared divisibility or prefix structure and supports a hierarchical topology.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ultrametric Hierarchy and Information","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"p adic valuation p adic valuation","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/p-Adic Valuation.md","fileName":"p-Adic Valuation.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"p-Adic Valuation","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Ultrametric Hierarchy and Information","datasciencefoundations_geometry.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}